# Dyadic each is currying (B6): `A f e_ach B` is `(f e_ach A) B`. When
# f applied to an item of A is itself a function, `f e_ach A` is a
# pending item-wise application, and B is zipped with it; a single
# value on either side extends to every item (T7).
== SOURCE
1 2 3 '+ e_ach 10 20 30
1 2 3 '= e_ach 1 5 3
5 '+ e_ach 1 2 3
1 2 3 '- e_ach 1
"abc" '= e_ach "abd"
3 1 4 '{ x y -> x < y ? x; y } e_ach 2 2 2
u:m_in2 := { x y -> x < y ? x; y }
(2 2 r_eshape 1 5 3 7) 'u:m_in2 e_ach 4
